Z||000000||doughboySE||01-21-2000||10:07 PM||||wow you guys are great thanx to everyone <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>not to show favortisim cause they all sound great but i think the setup im looking for is SPYDERS i love the thought of out of site out of mind.<BR>though i do have a few questions<BR>1- what the heck is a shaker <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>2- where is the instalation at the dead pedals?<BR>3-i love the foot well idea to how is that done exactually<BR>THIS WAS MY SETUP IN MY VW AND THIS IS WHAT I WANT IN THE FIERO<BR>6/10 off the 80w sony amp<BR>4/6 off the high power deack<BR>sub off the 100w mono pioneer amp<BR>LOOOOOOOOOOOTS OF BASE IT WAS POWERING A 12 INCH SAPHIRE SUB IN A PORTED BOX BEFORE.<BR>SPYDER do you have the box demensions? pics? and who was the person who said that the subs were installed in the false wall behind the seats? and any pics? <BR>thanx again fellows <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000001||Spyder||01-22-2000||01:32 PM||||Quick note: This one of the many ways to put a sub in a Fiero. This one is simple and inexpensive.<BR>A drawing:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/speakerbox.jpg"> <P>I don’t have the dimensions nor pictures of the boxes that I built (12 years ago), but here is what to do:<P>Since you’re going to install the sub behind the passenger seat, go sit in the seat, now see how comfortable you want your passengers to be.  Start measuring. Next, cut a board to go against the firewall and then make your other boards work off of it. Also put about a pound of poly-fill into the box.<P>Since your using a 100 watt amp:<BR>Sub woofer choices, Go with one with little power requirements but has high decibel ratings and made for the box you are building. (sealed of ported)<BR>The numbers say an 8” would be better, but I think I’d get a 10” speaker.<BR>Use a crossover at about 100hz (no more than 120hz no less 80hz)<BR>Also think about what you might add later, another box same size other side?...<BR>The Amp can be mounted  behind the drivers seat. Since I had boxes behind both seats I mounted the amp under the passenger side dash where the factory sub usually is. <BR>You can get poly-fill at Wal mart K mart, in the craft-sewing section, it’s pillow filler.<BR>Shakers: You know that feeling when the bass drops, well these things shake your seats with no sound, a vibrator.<P>If anyone would like to add anything else, feel free.<BR>||||reg||1
